Source: postgresql-q3c
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/segasai/q3c

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-q3c
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-q3c
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: ${postgresql:Breaks}
Description: PostgreSQL PGVERSION extension used for indexing the sky
 Q3C is designed for large astronomical catalogues and other catalogues of
 objects on a sphere. It provides fast circular, elliptical and polygonal
 searches, as well as fast cross-matches.
